 "notes": "The fighter's growth as the sim reads it (NP_11 s1, s3, s4, s6, s7, s9; NP_06 s1.2). The ability board: one hex-node layout per style archetype (4), 61 nodes in three lobes and a shared spine - the Body lobe's stat nodes (+2 / +3 / +5) and a soft-cap breaker per stat, the Craft lobe's passives, the Spirit lobe's Tension passives and its Anchor Wall (NP_05 s3's defensive board: the T2 walls learnable from the board, PAC-096), the spine's style nodes and the Boxer-Puncher's off-style socket - plus 2 nodes injected per named character, joined to the spine. A node is taken when it touches one already taken (the stance at the root is every fighter's, free), paid in Board Points (2 a level); a stat node whose stat stands at 70+ costs double unless that stat's breaker is taken. Respec is free at the gym from the Film Room's T2. Stat raises spend Beans (+1 = 5, then +1 a raise already bought on that stat), the stat's own typed Beans first, then the untyped; the training slots type their Beans by the game's bias, and a partner along flavours a quarter of them with his best stat. Rarity 1-4 (Club / Circuit / National / Legend) caps what growth can reach (70 / 80 / 90 / 99; a card's own stats stand as dressed), lifts a card's own total to the tier's (NP_11 s1, PAC-096) and ascends on Spirits (10 / 25 / 60) and a trial the fighter must do. Costs, layouts, the style splits of the craft passives, the named nodes and the trials are first drafts; the 9 passives are NP_11 s3's own, live on the sim; the other 31 of the 40-passive launch pool are the content lane's.",
